{
  "format": "rerail.policy/v1",
  "id": "eslint-plugin-vue-v-on-event-hyphenation",
  "revision": 1,
  "mode": "steer",
  "description": "Ports eslint-plugin-vue 10.11.1 `vue/v-on-event-hyphenation` with default options (always, ignore: [], ignoreTags: []): a static v-on argument (`@arg`, `v-on:arg`) on a component tag that contains an upper-case letter (value.toLowerCase() !== value) is reported at the directive attribute, with the whole key (modifiers included) in the message. The tree-sitter grammar splits `v-on:a:B` into `v-on:a` and `:B`; the `split-long-form` clause reads that case from the tag text. A tag is a component as eslint-plugin-vue utils.isCustomComponent decides: a static `is` attribute, `:is`/`v-bind:is`/`.is` or `v-is` (case-insensitive), or its raw tag name (case-sensitive) is not in the well-known list of its namespace (HTML, SVG under `<svg>`, MathML under `<math>`; namespace propagation follows vue-eslint-parser: foreignObject/desc/title and MathML text integration points switch children back to HTML); the element lists are the shared regexes in the `custom-tag` utility.",
